module avin

// A value that may be handed to another thread. The compiler decides it for every type from the
// type's structure, so it is written only as a bound, `[M: Sendable]`, or as a promise a declaration
// makes, `trait Shape: Sendable`, which every type implementing the trait is then checked to keep.
//
// Sendable are the scalars, `unit` and `string`; tuples and `data` types whose fields are all
// sendable; the immutable collections of sendable elements; a class that is neither `open` nor
// `abstract`, with no `var` field and only sendable fields, and an `object` likewise; a trait declared
// `: Sendable`, at sendable type arguments; the synchronized types (`Future`, `Promise`, `Channel` and
// `Atomic` of a sendable type, `Mutex` of any, `Once`); and Sysl handles, which a send hands over.
// Mutable collections, a class with a `var`, an `open` or `abstract` class, a function value and
// `Any` are not.
trait Sendable
